{"role":"user","content":"You need to read the Excel file at D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\4d0aa727-86b1-406b-9b33-f870dd14a4a5.xlsx and extract all its data.\n\nThe file contains information about locomotives owned by a railroad museum, with columns for: identifying number, operating status, and the name of the daily excursion it heads (if operational).\n\nPlease use the bash tool to run Python code to read this file. The working directory is D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia.\n\nTry this command:\n```\ncd /d D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia && python -c \"import openpyxl; wb=openpyxl.load_workbook('data/4d0aa727-86b1-406b-9b33-f870dd14a4a5.xlsx'); ws=wb.active; print('Sheet:', ws.title); [print(list(r)) for r in ws.iter_rows(values_only=True)]\"\n```\n\nIf that doesn't work, try alternative approaches like using pandas, or running python directly with the full path. If bash is completely blocked, try using the read tool with the file path.\n\nOnce you have the data, report back ALL rows and columns exactly as they appear in the file. Also identify:\n1. Which locomotives are assigned to the \"Sunset Picnic Trip\"\n2. Which of those are operational\n3. Which of those are steam locomotives (based on their type/designation)\n\nBe thorough and report the complete data."}
