{"role":"tool","content":"    1\t[\r\n    2\t {\r\n    3\t  \"task_id\": \"0383a3ee-47a7-41a4-b493-519bdefe0488\",\r\n    4\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n    5\t  \"file\": false,\r\n    6\t  \"question\": \"On the BBC Earth YouTube video of the Top 5 Silliest Animal Moments, what species of bird is featured?\",\r\n    7\t  \"gold\": \"Rockhopper penguin\",\r\n    8\t  \"got\": \"Rockhopper penguin\",\r\n    9\t  \"secs\": 19.9,\r\n   10\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Rockhopper penguin\\n\\n\"\r\n   11\t },\r\n   12\t {\r\n   13\t  \"task_id\": \"11af4e1a-5f45-467d-9aeb-46f4bb0bf034\",\r\n   14\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   15\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   16\t  \"question\": \"How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?\",\r\n   17\t  \"gold\": \"6\",\r\n   18\t  \"got\": \"6\",\r\n   19\t  \"secs\": 20.6,\r\n   20\t  \"raw_tail\": \" All You Need*:\\n\\n* **BERT Base Encoder:** Contains **12** encoder layers (transformer blocks).\\n* **Attention Is All You Need Encoder:** The original Transformer encoder architecture proposed by Vaswani et al. uses **6** encoder layers ($N = 6$).\\n\\nCalculating the difference:\\n$12 - 6 = 6$\\n\\nANSWER: 6\\n\\n\"\r\n   21\t },\r\n   22\t {\r\n   23\t  \"task_id\": \"23dd907f-1261-4488-b21c-e9185af91d5e\",\r\n   24\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   25\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   26\t  \"question\": \"In Audre Lorde\\u2019s poem \\u201cFather Son and Holy Ghost\\u201d, what is the number of the stanza in which some lines are indented?\",\r\n   27\t  \"gold\": \"2\",\r\n   28\t  \"got\": \"2\",\r\n   29\t  \"secs\": 15.2,\r\n   30\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 2\\n\\n\"\r\n   31\t },\r\n   32\t {\r\n   33\t  \"task_id\": \"27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c\",\r\n   34\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   35\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   36\t  \"question\": \"\\u00ac(A \\u2227 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2228 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acB \\u2192 \\u00acA)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 B)\\n(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n\\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full s\",\r\n   37\t  \"gold\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   38\t  \"got\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   39\t  \"secs\": 10.5,\r\n   40\t  \"raw_tail\": \"3, 4, and 6 are all valid logical equivalences (tautologies).\\nStatement 5, $(\\\\neg A \\\\rightarrow B) \\\\leftrightarrow (A \\\\lor \\\\neg B)$, is NOT a logical equivalence (it is invalid/contingent).\\n\\nThe question asks for the full statement that doesn't fit:\\n(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\nANSWER: (\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\n\"\r\n   41\t },\r\n   42\t {\r\n   43\t  \"task_id\": \"2d83110e-a098-4ebb-9987-066c06fa42d0\",\r\n   44\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   45\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   46\t  \"question\": \".rewsna eht sa \\\"tfel\\\" drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\",\r\n   47\t  \"gold\": \"Right\",\r\n   48\t  \"got\": \"right\",\r\n   49\t  \"secs\": 12.5,\r\n   50\t  \"raw_tail\": \" user's question is written in reverse text:\\n\\\".rewsna eht sa \\\"tfel\\\" drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\\\"\\n\\nReversed:\\n\\\"If you understand this sentence, write the opposite of the word \\\"left\\\" as the answer.\\\"\\n\\nThe opposite of \\\"left\\\" is \\\"right\\\".\\n\\nANSWER: right\\n\\n\\n[tool bash {}]\\n\"\r\n   51\t },\r\n   52\t {\r\n   53\t  \"task_id\": \"305ac316-eef6-4446-960a-92d80d542f82\",\r\n   54\t  \"level\": 1,\r\n   55\t  \"file\": false,\r\n   56\t  \"question\": \"Who did the actor who played Ray in the Polish-language version of Everybody Loves Raymond play in Magda M.? Give only the first name.\",\r\n   57\t  \"gold\": \"Wojciech\",\r\n   58\t  \"g