t Blount in 1974) to express distaste for the tamed and softened nature of dragon depictions in children's literature is **fluffy**.\\n\\nANSWER: fluffy\\n\\n\",\r\n  279\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  280\t },\r\n  281\t {\r\n  282\t  \"task_id\": \"bda648d7-d618-4883-88f4-3466eabd860e\",\r\n  283\t  \"question\": \"Where were the Vietnamese specimens described by Kuznetzov in Nedoshivina's 2010 paper eventually deposited? Just give me the city name without abbreviations.\",\r\n  284\t  \"gold\": \"Saint Petersburg\",\r\n  285\t  \"got\": \"Saint Petersburg\",\r\n  286\t  \"secs\": 10.8,\r\n  287\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Saint Petersburg\\n\\n\",\r\n  288\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  289\t },\r\n  290\t {\r\n  291\t  \"task_id\": \"c365c1c7-a3db-4d5e-a9a1-66f56eae7865\",\r\n  292\t  \"question\": \"Of the cities within the United States where U.S. presidents were born, which two are the farthest apart from the westernmost to the easternmost going east, giv\",\r\n  293\t  \"gold\": \"Braintree, Honolulu\",\r\n  294\t  \"got\": \"Braintree, Honolulu\",\r\n  295\t  \"secs\": 33.7,\r\n  296\t  \"raw_tail\": \"most to the easternmost:\\n\\n1. **Westernmost birth city:** **Honolulu**, Hawaii (birthplace of Barack Obama) at approximately $157.8583^\\\\circ\\\\text{ W}$ longitude.\\n2. **Easternmost birth city:** **Braintree**, Massachusetts (birthplace of John Adams and John Quincy Adams) at approximately $71.0023^\\\\circ\\\\text{ W}$ longitude.\\n\\nAlphabetically arranged: Braintree, Honolulu.\\n\\nANSWER: Braintree, Honolulu\\n\\n\",\r\n  297\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  298\t },\r\n  299\t {\r\n  300\t  \"task_id\": \"c714ab3a-da30-4603-bacd-d008800188b9\",\r\n  301\t  \"question\": \"You are Van Helsing, a renowned vampire hunter. A Count of Moldova, La\\u021bcu IV, son of  Costea, has tasked you with investigating the village of \\u0218irnea in neighbo\",\r\n  302\t  \"gold\": \"100\",\r\n  303\t  \"got\": \"100\",\r\n  304\t  \"secs\": 9.8,\r\n  305\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ition of the village is 0 humans and 100 vampires.\\n- Therefore, the statement *\\\"At least one of us is a human\\\"* is **false**.\\n- Since all residents are vampires, and vampires always lie, they *must* utter a false statement. Saying *\\\"At least one of us is a human\\\"* is a false statement, so vampires lying would naturally say it! \\n- Thus, all 100 residents can consistently be vampires.\\n\\nANSWER: 100\\n\\n\",\r\n  306\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  307\t },\r\n  308\t {\r\n  309\t  \"task_id\": \"cabe07ed-9eca-40ea-8ead-410ef5e83f91\",\r\n  310\t  \"question\": \"What is the surname of the equine veterinarian mentioned in 1.E Exercises from the chemistry materials licensed by Marisa Alviar-Agnew & Henry Agnew under the C\",\r\n  311\t  \"gold\": \"Louvrier\",\r\n  312\t  \"got\": \"\",\r\n  313\t  \"secs\": 11.5,\r\n  314\t  \"raw_tail\": \"Louvrier\\n\\n\",\r\n  315\t  \"correct\": false\r\n  316\t },\r\n  317\t {\r\n  318\t  \"task_id\": \"cf106601-ab4f-4af9-b045-5295fe67b37d\",\r\n  319\t  \"question\": \"What country had the least number of athletes at the 1928 Summer Olympics? If there's a tie for a number of athletes, return the first in alphabetical order. Gi\",\r\n  320\t  \"gold\": \"CUB\",\r\n  321\t  \"got\": \"CUB\",\r\n  322\t  \"secs\": 11.4,\r\n  323\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: CUB\\n\\n\",\r\n  324\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  325\t },\r\n  326\t {\r\n  327\t  \"task_id\": \"d0633230-7067-47a9-9dbf-ee11e0a2cdd6\",\r\n  328\t  \"question\": \"In the Scikit-Learn July 2017 changelog, what other predictor base command received a bug fix? Just give the name, not a path.\",\r\n  329\t  \"gold\": \"BaseLabelPropagation\",\r\n  330\t  \"got\": \"BaseLabelPropagation\",\r\n  331\t  \"secs\": 12.2,\r\n  332\t  \"raw_tail\": \"BaseLabelPropagation\\n\\nANSWER: BaseLabelPropagation\\n\\n\",\r\n  333\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  334\t },\r\n  335\t {\r\n  336\t  \"task_id\": \"dc22a632-937f-4e6a-b72f-ba0ff3f5ff97\",\r\n  337\t  \"question\": \"What was the complete title of the book in which two James Beard Award winners recommended the restaurant where Ali Khan enjoyed a New Mexican staple in his cos\",\r\n  338\t  \"gold\": \"Five Hundred Things To Eat Before It's Too Late: and the Very Best Places to Eat Them\",\r\n  339\t  \"got\": \"500 Things to Eat Before It's Too Late: and the Very Best Places to Eat Them\",\r\n  340\t  \"secs\": 16.9,\r\n  341\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 500 Things to Eat Before It's Too Late: and the Very Best Places to Eat Them\\n\\n\",\r\n  342\t  \"correct\": false\r\n  343\t },\r\n  344\t {\r\n  345\t  \"task_id\": \"dc28cf18-6431-458b-83ef-64b3ce566c10\",\r\n  346\t  \"question\": \"My family reunion is this week, and I was assigned the mashed potatoes to bring. The attendees include my married mother and father, my twin brother and his fam\",\r\n  347\t  \"gold\": \"2\",\r\n  348\t  \"got\": \"2\",\r\n  349\t  \"secs\": 11.3,\r\n  350\t  \"raw_tail\": \"erage potato is about half a pound, and potatoes are sold in 5-pound bags.\\\"\\n* Total weight of potatoes needed = $18 \\\\text{ potatoes} \\\\times 0.5 \\\\text{ lbs/potato} = 9 \\\\text{ pounds}$.\\n* Bag size = 5 pounds per bag.\\n* Number of bags = $9 / 5 = 1.8$ bags.\\n* Since you need whole bags (\\\"How many whole bags of potatoes do I need?\\\"), you must round up to the next whole bag, which is 2 bags.\\n\\nANSWER: 2\\n\\n\",\r\n  351\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  352\t },\r\n  353\t {\r\n  354\t  \"task_id\": \"e142056d-56ab-4352-b091-b56054bd1359\",\r\n  355\t  \"question\": \"Bob was invited to participate in a game show, and he advanced to the final round. The final round offered Bob the chance to win a large sum by playing a game a\",\r\n  356\t  \"gold\": \"16000\",\r\n  357\t  \"got\": \"16000\",\r\n  358\t  \"secs\": 19.7,\r\n  359\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 16000\\n\\n\\n[tool websearch {}]\\n\\n[tool websearch {\\\"query\\\":\\\"Bob was invited to participate in a game show and he advanced to the final round 30 shiny ]\\n\",\r\n  360\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  361\t },\r\n  362\t {\r\n  363\t  \"task_id\": \"e1fc63a2-da7a-432f-be78-7c4a95598703\",\r\n  364\t  \"question\": \"If Eliud Kipchoge could maintain his record-making marathon pace indefinitely, how many thousand hours would it take him to run the distance between the Earth a\",\r\n  365\t  \"gold\": \"17\",\r\n  366\t  \"got\": \"\",\r\n  367\t  \"secs\": 7.4,\r\n  368\t  \"raw_tail\": \"\\n\",\r\n  369\t  \"correct\": false\r\n  370\t },\r\n  371\t {\r\n  372\t  \"task_id\": \"ec09fa32-d03f-4bf8-84b0-1f16922c3ae4\",\r\n  373\t  \"question\": \"Here's a fun riddle that I think you'll enjoy.\\n\\nYou have been selected to play the final round of the hit new game show \\\"Pick That Ping-Pong\\\". In this round, yo\",\r\n  374\t  \"gold\": \"3\",\r\n  375\t  \"got\": \"3\",\r\n  376\t  \"secs\": 15.2,\r\n  377\t  \"raw_tail\": \"To maximize your odds of winning the grand prize, you should choose ball **3**.\\n\\nANSWER: 3\\n\\n\",\r\n  378\t  \"correct\": true\r\n  379\t }\r\n  380\t]","toolCallId":"call_97f9b457ba2f4529a0c67b43","name":"read"}
